  "extractionNotes": "Fixed-term employment 2024-04-10..2026-06-01, extended to the day of birth (employer remark); the child was born 2026-06-01, so maternity benefit after the employment, paid by ZUS. First ZAM and leave request: maternity 2026-06-01..2026-10-18 and parental 2026-10-19..2027-05-30 (father's statement of non-use for that period); Z-3 application date 2026-06-14 (day 13), so 81.5% is inferred. Term baby (box: born after 37 completed weeks) in hospital 2026-06-01..2026-06-29; second ZAM filed 2026-07-29 added supplementary maternity leave 2026-10-19..2026-11-15 (4 weeks) and moved parental to 2026-11-16..2027-06-28 (handwritten end on the ZAM reads 2027-06-26; the decision quotes 2027-06-28 = 225 days). ZUS decision (UZ art. 29a ust. 1): parental benefit for one child is 224 days, so the benefit for 2027-06-28 is refused; the rest was granted (case summary: maternity, supplementary and 32 weeks of parental). Hence two parental entries: 224 days granted and the excess day refused. Salary table (2024-11..2025-10) is partly illegible (6/8 confusion in every amount) and does not reach the months before the birth; months omitted, no base printed. She registered the child for health insurance herself. Payer-size box not legible. asOf = date of the second ZAM (decision undated in the scan)."
